STATES — faithful to the web source
  The web DetailCards receives health (useDrivetrainHealth), peakPower/avgPowerMax/minRegenPower (derived
  from useDrives) and stats (useDrivingStats) from its parent page, all asynchronous. The native superset
  owns those reads, so every mandated state renders: loading (skeleton cards), loaded (two cards), empty
  (no drivetrain-health snapshot — the web page's {health ? ... : <EmptyState/>} gate), error (retry),
  stale + offline (freshness chip + cached content). The web "Max Regen" row is reproduced exactly: the page
  hard-codes every chart powerMin to 0, so minRegenPower is never < 0 and the row is ALWAYS the em-dash —
  faithfully reproduced (not fabricated), documented in code + tested.

